From c56a8b8f1dde4b5b440436721a4fa993042e8725 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 10:07:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: vcnl4000: initialize ps_scale for
 vcnl4000/vcnl4010

For vcnl4000/vcnl4010, proximity raw reads return IIO_VAL_FRACTIONAL
but vcnl4000_init() leaves ps_scale uninitialized.

Reading the proximity sysfs attribute can then hit a zero denominator in
__iio_format_value(), causing repeated "Division by zero in kernel"
reports while userspace reads the channel.

Initialize ps_scale to 1 in vcnl4000_init() so fractional formatting
always has a valid denominator for these parts.

Fixes: 44b90383453c ("iio: light: vcnl4000: Set ps high definition for 4040/4200")
Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Assisted-by: GitHub Copilot:GPT-5.3-Codex
---
 drivers/iio/light/vcnl4000.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/light/vcnl4000.c b/drivers/iio/light/vcnl4000.c
index 128ae3f94074..70b9111f74a4 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/light/vcnl4000.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/light/vcnl4000.c
@@ -261,6 +261,7 @@ static int vcnl4000_init(struct vcnl4000_data *data)
 
 	data->rev = ret & 0xf;
 	data->al_scale = 250000;
+	data->ps_scale = 1;
 
 	return 0;
 };
-- 
